  "title": "Reference vs copy",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "md": "## Two names, one list\n\n`const b = a` does not copy items. Change `b[0]` and `a[0]` changes too. The fox will walk the surprise path if you mutate a shared route.\n\nCopy with `a.slice()` or `[...a]` when you mean a second list."
    },
    {
      "type": "predict",
      "id": "assign-copy",
      "promptMd": "After `const b = a; b[0] = \"south\"` (and `a` was `[\"east\"]`), `a[0]` is…",
      "kind": "mcq",
      "choices": [
        {
          "id": "east",
          "md": "`\"east\"` — assign copied",
          "misconceptionId": "arrays-are-copied-by-assign"
        },
        {
          "id": "south",
          "md": "`\"south\"` — both names point at one list"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "south"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "id": "shared-route",
      "engine": "javascript",
      "entry": "main.js",
      "promptMd": "> `shared` starts as `[\"east\",\"east\"]`. Another name mutates it to add `\"south\"`. Walk `shared` to (2, 1).",
      "files": [
        {
          "path": "files/main.js",
          "role": "edit"
        },
        {
          "path": "files/hidden.test.js",
          "role": "hidden-test"
        }
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "type": "js-assert"
        }
      ],
      "hintLadder": [
        {
          "level": 1,
          "kind": "concept",
          "md": "The comment marks the missing line: `also` has to gain a south step."
        },
        {
          "level": 2,
          "kind": "concept",
          "md": "`also` and `shared` are two names for one list, so pushing through either name changes both."
        },
        {
          "level": 3,
          "kind": "concept",
          "md": "`also.push(\"south\")` adds the step; the loop below already walks `shared`."
        },
        {
          "level": 4,
          "kind": "assist",
          "md": "const shared = [\"east\", \"east\"]\nconst also = shared\nalso.push(\"south\")\nfor (const d of shared) Player.move(d)\nmodule.exports = { shared }"
        }
      ],
